# Preact app

Preact client app on Vite+, deployed as Cloudflare static assets (`wrangler.jsonc`, SPA fallback).

- UI: cascivo first. `@cascivo/react` components and `--cascivo-*` tokens before own markup or CSS;
  shared components wrap cascivo in `packages/ui`. No Tailwind, CSS-in-JS or other component library.
- Preact renders cascivo client-side only (CSR): no SSR, no prerender.
- Look components up in https://cascivo.com/llms.txt (`llms-full.txt`) or the cascivo MCP server.
- Components come from `@cascivo/react` (prebuilt, React API) running on `preact/compat`: the
  Preact preset aliases `react` to `preact/compat`, `tsconfig.json` maps the same for types.
  `react` and `react-dom` are dev-only peers; `@preact/signals-react` is required by cascivo.
- Import a theme once in `src/main.tsx` (`@cascivo/themes/light-dark.css`); component CSS is automatic.
- Tests: `vp test run` with `happy-dom`; `vite.config.ts` inlines `@cascivo/*` so the alias applies.
  happy-dom lacks the Popover API: stub `showPopover`/`hidePopover` (cascivo `docs/TESTING.md` polyfills).
- `pnpm dev` serves on port 5173; `pnpm build` writes `dist/`.
{% if "ui-storybook" in pieces %}- Shared components: import from `@{{ scope }}/ui` (`workspace:*`, built by `vp pack`; turbo builds it first).
{% endif %}- Previews deploy to `<app>-preview` as alias `pr-<n>`. Never create `<app>-preview` by hand.
- Secrets set on the -preview Worker are readable by every PR.
- `kv`/`d1`/`r2`/`queue`/`service` ids in `env.preview` must be preview-only resources; previews share that data.
